# Brief 181 follow-up (2026-09-21).
#
# `scripts/deploy.sh` is executed by bash ON THE LINUX BOX. If it is ever
# checked out with CRLF endings, every line ends in a stray \r and the deploy
# dies on the first one with an unreadable error. This repo is developed on
# Windows and its two other .sh files are ALREADY stored with CRLF, so this is
# not hypothetical — it is the state the next new shell script would inherit.
#
# Scoped to this one path on purpose: renormalising the pre-existing scripts is
# a separate change and does not belong in a deploy-pipeline fix.
/scripts/deploy.sh text eol=lf
